ji'a lu ma'oste li'u cu lujvo fo lu cmavo liste li'u .i ji'a lu
gi'uste li'u .a lu gimste li'u cu lujvo fo lu gismu liste li'u

ni'o mi nelcu'a zo gi'uste mu'i lo du'u lo te morna be fi zo gi'uste
cu smimau lo te morna be fi zo ma'oste lo te morna be fi zo gimste

...which is probably bad Lojban, too, and I wasn't sure which word was
appropriate.

What I was trying to say is that I use {ma'oste} for the cmavo list
and {gi'uste} for the gismu list... even though {gimste} is the
canonical form for the lujvo, I prefer {gi'uste} because its
shape/form is more closely parallel to that of {ma'oste} (which has no
alternative with a CVC initial rafsi).

